"deviceId\",\"type\":\"bytes32\"},{\"internalType\":\"bytes32\",\"name\":\"prevCkpt\",\"type\":\"bytes32\"},{\"internalType\":\"bytes32\",\"name\":\"mmrRoot\",\"type\":\"bytes32\"},{\"internalType\":\"uint64\",\"name\":\"mmrSize\",\"type\":\"uint64\"},{\"internalType\":\"uint64\",\"name\":\"anchoredAt\",\"type\":\"uint64\"}],\"stateMutability\":\"view\",\"type\":\"function\"},{\"inputs\":[{\"internalType\":\"bytes32\",\"name\":\"deviceId\",\"type\":\"bytes32\"}],\"name\":\"submitterOf\",\"outputs\":[{\"internalType\":\"address\",\"name\":\"submitter\",\"type\":\"address\"}],\"stateMutability\":\"view\",\"type\":\"function\"}],\"devdoc\":{\"details\":\"Enforces only the signature-free rules of afir_anchor::AnchorLedger for one chain: per device, records link by prevCkpt from zero, mmrSize grows, an exact repeat is idempotent and a different record under an anchored id is a conflict. A device is bound once, by governance, to the address allowed to submit for it; that submitter can still publish garbage, which the offline audit rejects. No reward, stake or slash lives here.\",\"kind\":\"dev\",\"methods\":{\"anchor(bytes32,bytes32,bytes32,bytes32,uint64)\":{\"returns\":{\"newlyAnchored\":\"false for an exact repeat of an anchored record.\"}}},\"title\":\"AfirAnchor\",\"version\":1},\"userdoc\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"methods\":{},\"notice\":\"Publishes AFiR hybrid checkpoint roots (Arkhe AGI-P2P whitepaper v2.3, sections 9.2 and 9.4); chain half of I-09. Anchoring is publication, not verification: the EVM has no ML-DSA-65, Ed25519 or BLAKE3 precompile, so this contract never checks a checkpoint. Validity comes from the signed checkpoint, audited offline (arkhe-verify-core afir_anchor::audit).\",\"version\":1}},\"settings\":{\"compilationTarget\":{\"src/AfirAnchor.sol\":\"AfirAnchor\"},\"evmVersion\":\"cancun\",\"libraries\":{},\"metadata\":{\"bytecodeHash\":\"ipfs\"},\"optimizer\":{\"enabled\":true,\"runs\":200},\"remappings\":[]},\"sources\":{\"src/AfirAnchor.sol\":{\"kec